BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Black Mountain Democrats Read Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260821T070000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260821T080000
UID:041d2cc7cb50f0f5de4e96a1f7aeca73@mobilize.us
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://mobilize-uploads-prod.s3.amazonaws.com/u
 ploads/event/Black%20Mountain%20Democrats%20Read%20Book%20Club%20aug26_202
 60725003617014449.png
DESCRIPTION:Each month we discuss a book agreed upon at the previous meeti
 ng. The selection for August is "Politics Without Politicians: The Case fo
 r Citizen Rule\," written by Yale University professor Helene Landemore. I
 n the book Landemore argues that electoral politics is broken but democrac
 y isn't and "with sharp analysis and real-world examples...shows us how to
  move beyond democracy as a spectator sport\, embracing it as a shared pra
 ctice..." (Yale University website) Who should attend: Anyone who want
LOCATION:Peri Social House\, 406 W State St\, Black Mountain\, NC\, 28711
URL:https://www.mobilize.us/buncombedems/event/996907/
X-SOURCE:Buncombe County Democratic Party
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Black Mountain/Swannanoa-Riceville Meet-the-Candidates Picnic
